From: GPAP evaluation harness
Subject: [PATCH] cmsgen: --nowrite, --statsevery, --maxtime (GPAP eval only)

Three additions to meelgroup/cmsgen @ 8210aa9, all OFF by default (stock behaviour is
bit-identical unless the new flags are passed). They exist so a GPU-vs-CPU sampling
comparison can be made on equal terms; the measurements behind them are in GPAP's
docs/findings/RIVAL_FAIRNESS_FINDINGS.md (§1, §7).

  --nowrite       Generate the samples but emit none: no samplefile is opened, no sample is
                  formatted, and the every-10-samples console line is suppressed. This is the
                  apples-to-apples mode against GPAP's timed run, which likewise emits nothing
                  (its models stay on the GPU; delivery is a separate, off-timing pass).
                  Formatting full N-variable assignments is most of stock CMSGen's wall, and
                  the cost grows with |vars|, so it is largest exactly on the big circuit
                  unrolls.

  --statsevery N  Print `c gpap-stats samples=.. props=.. decisions=.. conflicts=.. cpu_s=..
                  wall_s=..` every N samples (default 1000) and once at the end, flushed, so a
                  harness that kills the process on a time budget still sees every completed
                  line. props/decisions are CryptoMiniSat's own counters
                  (SATSolver::get_sum_propagations/decisions/conflicts) — the CPU numbers that
                  GPAP's impl/s and dec/s columns are compared against.

  --maxtime N     Stop sampling after N seconds and exit NORMALLY through the same code path a
                  completed run takes, so the final `c gpap-stats ... final=1` line is printed
                  with an EXACT sample count. Without it a harness enforcing a per-instance time
                  budget has to kill the process, and everything sampled since the last
                  --statsevery line is lost: a killed run reports a multiple of the cadence, and
                  "sampled nothing" can mean "sampled fewer than N". The budget is armed per
                  solve() call (CMS resets conf.maxTime on return) and measures the SAMPLING
                  loop, not parsing.

Apply with:  git apply /path/to/cmsgen_gpap_eval.patch   (scripts/build_cmsgen.sh does it)

